	 To register and vote, you must: 

 Be a U.S. citizen 
 Be a resident of Idaho and Gem County for thirty (30) days preceding the election 
 Have reached eighteen (18) years of age 

 To register to vote, you must provide one of the following acceptable forms of identification: 

 Current Idaho Driver's License 
 Current Idaho Identification Card 
 Current U.S. Passport or Federal Photo Identification 
 Current Tribal Identification Card 
 Current Idaho Concealed Weapons License  

 To register to vote, you must provide one of the following items for proof of residence: 

 Photo ID w/ Correct Address 
 Proof of Insurance 
 Mortgage, Lease or Rental Agreement 
 Property Tax Assessment, Bill, or Receipt 
 Utility Bill (NO Cell Phone Bills) 
 Bank/Credit Card Statement 
 Paystub/Paycheck 
 Intake Document to Care Facility 
 Enrollment Letter From Idaho HS or University 
 Letter from Social Service Agency 

 You are not eligible to vote if you have been: 

 Convicted of a felony and your rights have not been restored. 

 You need to register again if you have: 

 Changed your name 
 Moved to a different address 
 Not voted within the last four (4) years 

 You may register to vote online at:   voteidaho.gov If you need to cancel your voter registration complete the form below.  Cancellation of Voter Registration 
 You may also register to vote by completing a  Voter Registration Form  and mailing it or in person at: Gem County Clerk Gem County Courthouse 415 E. Main St.  Room 202 Emmett, ID 83617 Monday through Friday 8:00am – 5:00pm Registration is subject to dates on the  Current Local Elections Calendar 
 SAME DAY REGISTRATION In Idaho we also have same day registration, which gives you the privilege to register on Election Day. In order to register and vote on Election Day you must: 

 Appear in person 
 Have a acceptable photo ID and an acceptable form of proof of 30-day residency such as a:

 Drivers license 
 Idaho ID card 
 Acceptable proof of residency document which contains a valid address in the precinct you reside with 



 NOTE:  When going to the polls to vote, you will need to have a state or federal issued  photo ID . 
 Call the Clerk’s Office at (208) 365-4561 if you have questions. 
 

		 
	 
	 


 
 

